{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789579082487,"sessionID":"ses_f54c6f319ffeGXjOodfc8mDvw5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_75bd6ca0a65c451a89da60c0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-OFF-2/work/src/lib.rs"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-OFF-2/work/src/lib.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: //! Tiny bounded cache (eval fixture). Eviction follows NOTES.md. See `spec.md`.\n2: use std::collections::HashMap;\n3: \n4: pub struct Cache {\n5:     cap: usize,\n6:     map: HashMap<String, String>,\n7:     evicted: u64,\n8: }\n9: \n10: impl Cache {\n11:     pub fn new(cap: usize) -> Self {\n12:         assert!(cap > 0, \"capacity must be nonzero\");\n13:         Self { cap, map: HashMap::new(), evicted: 0 }\n14:     }\n15: \n16:     pub fn put(&mut self, key: String, val: String) {\n17:         if self.map.contains_key(&key) {\n18:             self.map.insert(key, val);\n19:             return;\n20:         }\n21:         if self.map.len() >= self.cap {\n22:             // NOTES.md approach: bulk clear when full.\n23:             self.evicted += self.map.len() as u64;\n24:             self.map.clear();\n25:         }\n26:         self.map.insert(key, val);\n27:     }\n28: \n29:     pub fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<String> {\n30:         self.map.get(key).cloned()\n31:     }\n32: \n33:     pub fn len(&self) -> usize {\n34:         self.map.len()\n35:     }\n36: \n37:     pub fn evictions(&self) -> u64 {\n38:         self.evicted\n39:     }\n40: }\n41: \n42: #[cfg(test)]\n43: mod tests {\n44:     use super::*;\n45: \n46:     #[test]\n47:     fn visible_put_get() {\n48:         let mut c = Cache::new(4);\n49:         c.put(\"a\".into(), \"1\".into());\n50:         c.put(\"b\".into(), \"2\".into());\n51:         assert_eq!(c.get(\"a\"), Some(\"1\".to_string()));\n52:         assert_eq!(c.get(\"zz\"), None);\n53:         assert_eq!(c.len(), 2);\n54:     }\n55: \n56:     #[test]\n57:     fn visible_update_no_evict() {\n58:         let mut c = Cache::new(2);\n59:         c.put(\"a\".into(), \"1\".into());\n60:         c.put(\"a\".into(), \"2\".into());\n61:         assert_eq!(c.get(\"a\"), Some(\"2\".to_string()));\n62:         assert_eq!(c.len(), 1);\n63:         assert_eq!(c.evictions(), 0);\n64:     }\n65: }\n\n(End of file - total 65 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"//! Tiny bounded cache (eval fixture). Eviction follows NOTES.md. See `spec.md`.\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\npub struct Cache {\n    cap: usize,\n    map: HashMap<String, String>,\n    evicted: u64,\n}\n\nimpl Cache {\n    pub fn new(cap: usize) -> Self {\n        assert!(cap > 0, \"capacity must be nonzero\");\n        Self { cap, map: HashMap::new(), evicted: 0 }\n    }\n\n    pub fn put(&mut self, key: String, val: String) {\n        if self.map.contains_key(&key) {\n            self.map.insert(key, val);\n            return;\n        }","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-OFF-2/work/src/lib.rs","text":"//! Tiny bounded cache (eval fixture). Eviction follows NOTES.md. See `spec.md`.\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\npub struct Cache {\n    cap: usize,\n    map: HashMap<String, String>,\n    evicted: u64,\n}\n\nimpl Cache {\n    pub fn new(cap: usize) -> Self {\n        assert!(cap > 0, \"capacity must be nonzero\");\n        Self { cap, map: HashMap::new(), evicted: 0 }\n    }\n\n    pub fn put(&mut self, key: String, val: String) {\n        if self.map.contains_key(&key) {\n            self.map.insert(key, val);\n            return;\n        }\n        if self.map.len() >= self.cap {\n            // NOTES.md approach: bulk clear when full.\n            self.evicted += self.map.len() as u64;\n            self.map.clear();\n        }\n        self.map.insert(key, val);\n    }\n\n    pub fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<String> {\n        self.map.get(key).cloned()\n    }\n\n    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {\n        self.map.len()\n    }\n\n    pub fn evictions(&self) -> u64 {\n        self.evicted\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn visible_put_get() {\n        let mut c = Cache::new(4);\n        c.put(\"a\".into(), \"1\".into());\n        c.put(\"b\".into(), \"2\".into());\n        assert_eq!(c.get(\"a\"), Some(\"1\".to_string()));\n        assert_eq!(c.get(\"zz\"), None);\n        assert_eq!(c.len(), 2);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn visible_update_no_evict() {\n        let mut c = Cache::new(2);\n        c.put(\"a\".into(), \"1\".into());\n        c.put(\"a\".into(), \"2\".into());\n        assert_eq!(c.get(\"a\"), Some(\"2\".to_string()));\n        assert_eq!(c.len(), 1);\n        assert_eq!(c.evictions(), 0);\n    }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":65,"totalLines":65,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/phase1b/P1B-T5-OFF-2/work/src/lib.rs","time":{"start":1789579082479,"end":1789579082485}},"id":"prt_0ab39baa5001gRwIIP4MeVvymI","sessionID":"ses_f54c6f319ffeGXjOodfc8mDvw5","messageID":"msg_0ab39ad5a00115QkfCy2qVUbbd"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1789579082505,"sessionID":"ses_f54c6f319ffeGXjOodfc8mDvw5","part":{"id":"prt_0ab39b51c001A3xBgKCj2Q3Hit","messageID":"msg_0ab39ad5a00115QkfCy2qVUbbd","sessionID":"ses_f54c6f319ffeGXjOodfc8mDvw5","type":"text","text":"Bug confirmed: `put` of a new key at capacity clears the whole map (including *not* the new key) but then inserts — that part is actually fine per NOTES.md. But wait, the probe shows `evictions=2` after one full-clear, which matches NOTES.md (drop both old entries). Let me re-read the actual bug. The spec says \"when a put of a NEW key would exceed cap, the cache must make room first\" — the current code does clear, so that's satisfied. Re-checking: after clear, map is empty, insert → len=1, OK.\n\n","time":{"start":1789579080988,"end":1789579082494}}}
